---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import UiLabel from "../../components/UiLabel.astro";
import HelpCard from "../../components/HelpCard.astro";

// Issue #1106, guide 3: inviting someone, written as separate
// walk-throughs for both directions — inviting a guardian into a profile
// you track on, and inviting the profile's subject to log it herself.
// Positioning rule (docs/product/positioning.md): the two directions get
// equal weight and neither is framed as the default. Screen names and
// button labels come from the app's ARB strings through <UiLabel>, the
// invitation mechanics reuse the in-app help cards, and every factual
// claim carries a `<!-- cite: ... -->` ledger entry checked by
// `site/scripts/check-claims.mjs`.
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Inviting someone"
  description="Two walk-throughs: invite a guardian into a profile you track on, or set a profile up for someone and invite her to log it herself. Invitations are single-use links that expire."
>
  <article class="doc">
    <h1 class="doc__title">Inviting someone</h1>
    <p class="doc__lede">
      Sharing always starts with one person creating a single-use
      invitation link, and ends with the other person opening it and
      accepting. Families arrive from both directions, so this guide is
      two walk-throughs — read the one that is you, or both.
    </p>
    <section>
      <h2>How an invitation works</h2>
      <HelpCard id="invitations" />
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>You track for yourself, and invite someone in</h2>
      <p>
        Sam has been logging her own cycle and wants her partner Alex to
        follow along and help log. Alex needs his own lunarlog account on
        his own device; the invitation carries him in.
      </p>
      <ol class="doc__steps">
        <li>
          Open the profile's guardian management: from the profile, choose
          <UiLabel key="profilePickerMenuGuardians" />.
          <!-- cite: lib/ui/sharing/manage_guardians_screen.dart; lib/l10n/app_en.arb (profilePickerMenuGuardians) -->
        </li>
        <li>
          Choose <UiLabel key="sharingManageGuardiansInviteAction" />. The
          invitation is created from your lunarlog account, so sign in
          first if the app asks.
          <!-- cite: lib/ui/sharing/invite_guardian_dialog.dart; lib/l10n/app_en.arb (firstRunInviteWhyAccount) -->
        </li>
        <li>
          Pick the role the invitation carries — the person accepting
          cannot choose a higher one than you sent. Alex gets
          <UiLabel key="guardianRoleLabelCoParent" /> so he can log and
          manage alongside Sam; a <UiLabel
            key="guardianRoleLabelCaregiver"
          /> link is the fit when someone should log but not manage, and a
          <UiLabel key="guardianRoleLabelViewer" /> link for read-only.
          <!-- cite: lib/domain/help/help_cards.dart (invitations card); lib/ui/sharing/invite_guardian_dialog.dart (role picker) -->
        </li>
        <li>
          Share the link the app shows —
          <UiLabel
            key="inviteCreatedShareGuardian"
            values={{ profile: "Sam" }}
          />
          It works once and expires; Alex can open it on his phone and
          accept.
          <!-- cite: lib/ui/sharing/invite_guardian_dialog.dart (created-link share step); lib/domain/help/help_cards.dart (invitations card: single-use, 48h) -->
        </li>
        <li>
          On Alex's side, opening the link shows
          <UiLabel key="sharingAcceptInviteTitle" /> with the role spelled
          out; <UiLabel key="sharingAcceptInviteAccept" /> brings Sam's
          profile onto his device, syncing from then on. Until he accepts,
          the pending invitation sits in the guardian management list,
          where Sam can cancel it with
          <UiLabel key="manageGuardiansCancelInviteTooltip" />.
          <!-- cite: lib/ui/sharing/accept_invite_sheet.dart; lib/ui/sharing/manage_guardians_screen.dart (pending list + cancel) -->
        </li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        What Alex sees is the whole profile, under his role — the same
        entries, estimates, and history Sam sees, in guardian view.
        <!-- cite: PRIVACY.md#5-minors-privacy--family-profiles (accepted guardians read what is logged) -->
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>You set a profile up for someone, and invite her to log it</h2>
      <p>
        Dana's daughter Maya is fifteen and wants to keep her own log.
        Dana creates the profile on her own phone, logs the early days
        while Maya settles in, and then hands Maya the invitation — from
        then on Maya logs on her own phone, and Dana follows along.
      </p>
      <ol class="doc__steps">
        <li>
          Create the profile: <UiLabel key="profilePickerAddProfileTooltip"
          /> from <UiLabel key="profilePickerTitle" />, and on
          <UiLabel key="firstRunWhoLabel" /> choose
          <UiLabel key="firstRunWhoSomeone" />. Mark
          <UiLabel key="firstRunMinorLabel" /> for a young person — it
          keeps the framing right for her age.
          <!-- cite: lib/ui/profiles/first_run_screen.dart (someone-I-care-for path, minor flag) -->
        </li>
        <li>
          In the new profile's guardian management, choose
          <UiLabel key="sharingManageGuardiansInviteAction" /> and pick the
          option addressed to the person the profile is about:
          <UiLabel key="inviteSubjectOption" values={{ name: "Maya" }} />.
          <!-- cite: lib/ui/sharing/invite_guardian_dialog.dart (subject invitation option, inviteSubjectOption) -->
        </li>
        <li>
          Share the link with Maya:
          <UiLabel key="inviteCreatedShareSubject" values={{ name: "Maya" }} />
          On her phone, she signs in — or creates her account — and
          accepts. Her screen says it plainly:
          <UiLabel key="acceptInviteSubjectIntro" values={{ profile: "Maya" }} />
          <!-- cite: lib/ui/sharing/accept_invite_sheet.dart (subject intro, acceptInviteSubjectIntro); lib/ui/sharing/invite_guardian_dialog.dart (created-link share step) -->
        </li>
        <li>
          From then on the profile is hers to log on her own device, with
          Dana's access exactly as she chose it. Maya is the profile's
          subject and logs it; Dana remains its guardian — the
          <a href="/guides/transferring-ownership/">ownership transfer</a>
          is a separate, later decision, not a requirement for any of
          this.
          <!-- cite: docs/product/positioning.md (ownership transfer is a separate, later decision); lib/ui/sharing/invite_guardian_dialog.dart (subject invitation = caregiver access) -->
        </li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        A young person accepting an invitation sees an age note as part of
        the setup — lunarlog is licensed 13 and up, and a parent or
        guardian's invitation is how a younger teenager uses it.
        <!-- cite: PRIVACY.md#5-minors-privacy--family-profiles (minimum age); lib/ui/profiles/first_run_screen.dart (parent-invite age acknowledgement, firstRunAgeAcknowledgementParentInviteLabel) -->
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Changing your mind</h2>
      <p>
        An invitation that has not been used can be cancelled from the
        same guardian management list. A guardian who is already in can be
        removed there too — removal ends their access immediately and
        cancels every still-open invitation for that profile; the entries
        they logged stay, with their original attribution.
      </p>
      <HelpCard id="revocation" />
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
